by nicolas-grekas at 2026-09-28T08:29:00Z

I pushed a few changes: an assignment that always runs now replaces the previous values of the variable instead of adding to them (so `$key = 'foo'; $key = $other;` doesn't extract `foo` anymore, and reusing a variable doesn't attach the second call to the first key), `parent::` calls from classes that can't be autoloaded are skipped instead of throwing, and resolving the classes a variable may hold is memoized (it was exponential with variables copied in branches).

One question remains: method resolution doesn't care about the extracted paths, so extracting `Security/Http` finds "An authentication exception occurred." from `AuthenticationException::getMessageKey()` in Security/Core. In an app, that means vendor-owned messages land in the app's catalogue with the `__` prefix and then override the vendor translations. Should we resolve only methods declared in files under the extracted paths? WDYT?

