by guillaume-sainthillier at 2026-09-28T08:36:44Z

Thanks for the fixes! Agreed on the vendor question: pushed 89c068b311f, which reads method bodies only from files under the paths given to `extract()`. Types are still resolved through reflection, so `$vendorObject->getStatus()->label()` keeps working when `label()` is in the app. Extracting `Security/Http` alone no longer finds Core's message.

The method cases moved to their own fixture directory and test, and the limitations fixture documents the new rule. One trade-off: `translation:extract` calls `extract()` once per code path, so a PHP template under `templates/` won't resolve methods of classes living in `src/`. That looked acceptable to me, since PHP templates are rare.

